; aluminosilicate mineral with layered structure. plastic when wet, hard when fired.
; water enters between silicate layers → layers slide → material deforms.
; firing (sintering at 800-1200°C): water leaves, layers bond → ceramic.
; 
; properties:
; plastic when wet: coefficient of restitution ≈ 0 (perfectly inelastic)
; deformable without fracture (unlike brittle materials)
; fired clay (ceramic): hard (7 Mohs), brittle, chemically inert
; low thermal conductivity in wet form
; ion exchange: clay particles carry negative charge → hold nutrients in soil
; 
; types: kaolinite (white clay, porcelain), montmorillonite (swelling clay),
; illite (common soil clay), smectite (cat litter, drilling mud).

